# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Editors — deliberately unanchored (ADR-0063 point 2, anchoring audit
# 2026-08-18): no single "the" editor-config directory is a named kind here,
# and any nested project/fixture may legitimately carry its own .vscode/.idea/,
# so depth-unbounded matching is the intended behavior, not an oversight.
.vscode/
.idea/

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (never commit)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent tool worktree-isolated dispatch directories (isolation: "worktree"),
# e.g. .claude/worktrees/agent-<id>/ — never a deliverable, must never block
# Full Verify's VERIFY-CANDIDATE-PREFLIGHT.
.claude/worktrees/

# Private Overlay and machine-local marketplace/account/path mapping. The public
# setup compiler consumes only private-overlay.yaml's anonymous immutable Shared SHA.
.pipeline/private-overlay.yaml
.pipeline/machine-local.yaml

# Temp / scratch
*.log
*.tmp
stdin_dump.json
tmp-inbounds.txt
# ANCHORED 2026-08-18 (ADR-0063 point 2, anchoring audit): scratch/'s one
# stated home is the repo root (docs/adr/0063-repository-directory-contract.md).
# Onboarding's own consumer-project seed already writes this entry anchored
# (project-onboarding-v3.mjs PROJECT_IGNORE_SEED, "/scratch/" not "scratch/"),
# with the exact same one-character omission that once let unanchored
# `evidence/` swallow `backlog/evidence/` named as the reason why. The source
# repo that teaches consumers the anchored form must not carry the unanchored
# one itself.
/scratch/

# Machine-generated verify evidence (QG-03, AC-G4-2): regenerated every
# `node harness/scripts/verify.mjs` run — a status snapshot, not a durable
# audit trail (unlike .claude/guard-override.log.jsonl), so it stays out of history.
#
# ANCHORED 2026-08-09. Without the leading slash this rule matched an `evidence`
# directory at ANY depth, so it also swallowed `backlog/evidence/` — the one
# location the backlog closure contract requires `closure_evidence` to live in —
# and `specs/*/evidence/`, where Critic verdicts and dispatch records are filed.
# Already-tracked files stayed visible because git does not re-evaluate ignore
# rules against them, so the rule only ever ate NEW evidence: a closure could
# cite a file no other checkout can resolve, and the one that got through did so
# via `git add -f`. Only the machine-generated root directory was ever meant.
/evidence/

# Dispatch records written to the repository ROOT instead of `evidence/`. Anchored,
# so it never touches `evidence/dispatch-record-*.json`, which is where the template
# (`templates/prompts/goldfish-task.md` field 6) says these belong. 26 of them were
# tracked here until 2026-09-01: a dispatch wrote its record to the working directory
# and a broad `git add` in the same commit swept it into unrelated feature work — the
# clearest case being `55912293`, "per-task dispatch-record naming", which committed a
# bare `dispatch-record.json` to the root in the very commit that introduced the naming
# convention. None was ever cited as `closure_evidence`; they were archived, not deleted.
# The rule exists so the same accident cannot re-enter history silently.
/dispatch-record.json
/dispatch-record-*.json

# Bounded non-authoritative restart aid. It is local context, never project
# authority or a deliverable, so it must not dirty a candidate or enter history.
project/resume-hint.json

# Per-session context-budget snapshot (statusline-context.mjs) and Stop-hook suggestion
# dedup/nag-cap marker (stop-suggest.mjs) — machine-regenerated per session_id, never a
# durable audit trail, plan `.claude/plans/2026-07-07-retro-speed.md` package G-B.
.claude/.usage-*.json
.claude/.stop-suggest-*.json
.claude/.pipeline-install-consent-*.json
# Per-session model-identity evidence (43a8c799) — same class as the three above:
# machine-regenerated per session_id, never a durable audit trail. It shipped
# without an ignore rule, so every session left an untracked file that made
# verify.mjs's candidate preflight reject the tree as dirty before a single suite
# ran (`binding: preflight-rejected`) — the same unsatisfiable-gate shape already
# recorded above for `/evidence/`.
.claude/.main-session-model-identity-*.json
*.usage-*.json
*.stop-suggest-*.json

# Local environment overrides (never commit secrets)
.env

# Machine-generated append-only logs — EXCEPT the guard-override ledger, which
# guardrails/git.md keeps committed as the durable audit trail (so negate it here).
*.jsonl
!.claude/guard-override.log.jsonl

# NVA-A8 benchmark workload runtime output: each fixed workload's task.mjs
# overwrites this on every run (nova-a8-benchmark-runner.mjs); regenerated,
# never a deliverable.
plugins/pipeline-core/scripts/fixtures/nova-benchmark/workloads/*/result.txt
